type":"text","text":"The screenshot is included inline as a base64-encoded PNG in the image content entry above (mimeType: image/png).\nIt is also hosted at the URL in the first content entry (as JSON). To download a copy:\n\n  curl -f -L -o screenshot.png \"https://www.figma.com/api/mcp/asset/f0f8ddac-827b-4611-a91f-0cadc99ec60d.png\"\n\nThe URL returns raw PNG bytes (Content-Type: image/png). The URL is short-lived — treat it like a secret."}],"_meta":{"mcpRequestId":"cfd3f4f6-eebf-4c15-950c-c380998e4fc3"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01TWHpAakNFtEQtctrsFRLdE","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ym3fv3gg3z5zuo35lbcihxxgmgacy4p7owp3l4vy5ptru33yyo6q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":26,"cache_creation_input_tokens":903,"cache_read_input_tokens":129811,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":903,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ba07249-fdf3-45be-bb3a-d8082a07ab07","uuid":"f7764394-d5a1-46d1-a492-7a8f9c428c33","timestamp":"2026-10-31T22:10:42.916Z","thinking_duration_ms":7750}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ym3fv3gg3z5zuo35lbcihxxgmgacy4p7owp3l4vy5ptru33yyo6q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 8 Meet screens, their components and the prototype are built in **03 · Workspace**. I took a screenshot of every screen and fixed the problems I found. I worked as zuohaosheng@tetras.ai (confirmed with whoami), and the reference pages 00, 01, 02 and 04 were not changed.\n\n**File:** https://www.figma.com/design/jNSdbcJkhQYP0D5JB5bGQn/\n**03 · Workspace page ID:** `7:2`\n\n| Frame | ID |\n|---|---|\n| 01_Welcome | `21:166` |\n| 02_Apple_ID_Sheet | `22:189` |\n| 03_Explore | `26:228` |\n| 04_Find_Partner | `29:356` |\n| 05_Friend_Profile | `30:485` |\n| 06_Short_Video | `31:633` |\n| 07_Profile | `30:582` |\n| 08_Menu | `31:728` |\n\n**Design system** (in the frame \"Meet · Components\", `10:2`):\n- **Styles:** a color variable collection with the two brand colors plus my own neutrals, surfaces, scrim and semantic colors (online, like, error, disabled). There are also 13 Inter text styles and effect styles for card, bar and sheet shadows and a glass blur.\n- **Components and states:**\n  - Tab Bar: current tab Home / Dating / Profile / None\n  - Profile Tabs: current Top / Recent / Short\n  - Headers: Explore, Back, Back + More, Menu, and a dark version for the Short\n  - Buttons: small buttons in Default / Pressed / Disabled / Following; large buttons built on the Button from 02; Google and Facebook buttons\n  - Like / pass / super like buttons, each with a pressed state\n  - Story Avatar: Your Story / Unseen / Seen\n  - Feed Post: Default / Liked\n  - Swipe Card: top card and cards behind\n  - Also: Profile Header (friend / me), Media Tile (photo / video with play badge), Short overlay (Default / Liked), Menu Row, Quick Action, Apple ID Sheet and Menu Drawer\n- All photos, the logo and the icons are instances from 04 · Media, and each person uses their own portrait. All copy and data come verbatim from the brief.\n\n**Prototype:** all 17 required links are wired, and the flow starts at 01_Welcome.\n- 01 Sign Up opens 02 as a sheet sliding up. In 02, Face ID goes to 03 and close goes back to 01.\n- In 03, Claire's story goes to 05, the Dating tab to 04 and the Profile tab to 07.\n- In 04, back and the Home tab go to 03, and the Profile tab goes to 07.\n- In 05, back goes to 03 and the Short tab goes to 06. In 06, back goes to 05.\n- In 07, the menu opens 08 as a drawer and the Home tab goes to 03. In 08, close and Show Profile go back to 07.\n\n**Limitations:**\n- **Links use invisible tap areas.** Figma didn't save links set directly on layers inside instances (it reported no error). So the tabs, the back/menu buttons, the Short tab, the sheet's Face ID and close, and the drawer's close and Show Profile are each linked from a transparent \"Hotspot/…\" layer placed on top of them.\n- **Sheet and drawer are separate screens.** 02 and 08 are full frames showing a dimmed copy of 01 or 07 behind the sheet or drawer, with a slide transition, rather than Figma overlays.\n- **Scrolling is unconfirmed.** 03, 05 and 07 scroll inside the 852 px screen, with the header and tab bar meant to stay fixed. I haven't played the prototype to confirm the fixed parts behave correctly. Screenshots only show the first screen of content, so the lower feed posts and the bottom row of the grids aren't visible in them.\n- **Feed posts have no counts.** Like, comment and more appear without numbers because the brief gives no counts for posts.\n- **Translucent fills aren't tied to color variables.** On instances, Figma reset the opacity of variable-linked fills to 100%. So the glass and scrim fills use plain colors set to the same values, not variables."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":26,"cache_creation_input_tokens":903,"cache_read_input_tokens":129811,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_inp